infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Event-loop lag: the mean hides what the tail reveals
  desc Same measurement window — the average says "fine", the percentile says "on fire"
  compares
    - label Mean: the comfortable lie
      children
        - label Mean reports ~2 ms
          desc A genuine average — most ticks really are near-zero
        - label Drowns spikes in thousands of tiny samples
          desc A handful of 300 ms blocks per minute barely move it
        - label Answers "a typical tick"
          desc Not the stalls the unlucky requests actually feel
    - label Tail p99 / max: what users feel
      children
        - label p99 / max reads 400 ms (same window)
          desc The metric that tracks real user pain — alert on it
        - label Read off a nanosecond histogram
          desc monitorEventLoopDelay keeps the full distribution
        - label Speaks for the unlucky 1% of callbacks
          desc Exactly the population tail latency is made of
theme
  palette #f43f5e #14b8a6
